A||||7||DJRice||F-body Seat Swap Pics||||6||
Z||000000||DJRice||01-16-2000||10:56 PM||||There have been many questions about seat covers and the like.  After trying several seat covers and not being pleased, I went seat hunting at my local bone yard.  I ended up with one set of tan seats out of a 97 Firebird, and one set of Grey Seats out of a Camaro (96 I think).  The swap itself is simple, but I did it over a year ago and didnt take pictures of the acutal installation, but here is what they look like installed.  The F-body rails are easily removed from the seat assembly as they are only held on by 4 10mm nuts.  The original Fiero Seat rails will bolt right up.  This is a very simple mod.  And as you can see, they look good too.<P> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat1.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat2.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat3.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat4.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat5.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat6.jpg"> <BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/seat7.jpg"> <P>||||reg||6
Z||000001||DaRkLoRD||01-17-2000||12:29 AM||||Those look awesome!<BR>I love the look and smell of leather seats/seat covers, but it'd be far too hot in the summer. One of my dads old cars had leather seats, and any time you were in the car in the summer you had to peel yourself off the seats. hated it.<P>How much did those grey seats cost?||||reg||1
Z||000002||DJRice||01-17-2000||08:27 AM||||Actually, I got a sweet deal on those seats.  $75 for each <B><I>pair!</I></B><BR>They are really nice firm seats.||||reg||1
Z||000003||ChadMan||01-17-2000||08:34 AM||||Those look fantastic.  Is it any harder to use your emergency brake than it was with the factory seats?||||reg||14
Z||000004||Eric||01-17-2000||07:06 PM||||Did you notice if the seats were any wider across the bottom?||||reg||1
Z||000005||stimpy||01-17-2000||08:01 PM||||Do you lose any headroom with these seats? I am 6'6" so I don't have any to lose, but otherwise it sounds like a sweet set-up.  And the Camaro/Firebird recycler is on my way home, hmmmm...||||reg||1
Z||000006||DJRice||01-18-2000||08:27 AM||||The E-brake is just as convienient to use as it was before.  As for the size of the seat, if I had to guess I would say that the seat frames are probably very close to identical.<BR>Actually, the installing the grey set did cost a bit of head room because they have an extra adjustment that raises the back up a bit.  The tan seats didnt have that feature so I think that if you get seats that dont have that on it, youll be fine.<P>Im glad you guys like them, I know I was pretty proud of how well both sets fit and look.||||reg||1
Z||000007||ChadMan||01-18-2000||08:41 AM||||I feel like a sucker now, having paid $100 for one original seat.  Good find, DJ.||||reg||1
